Art Willis <nhplayer@trantor.nospam.com> writes:
> If you have teleport control, is it possible to level teleport
> between dungeon branches, such as you can with the Eye of Mispelling?
> E.g. between main dungeon and Minetown, or vice versa.

In a few cases, and in a specific direction, only.

Gnomish Mines -> levels of the Dungeons of Doom above the Mines.
Sokoban -> levels of the Dungeons of Doom higher than Sokoban's top level.
Dungeons of Doom -> Valley of the Dead.
Gehennom -> Dungeons of Doom.
Vlad's Tower -> levels of Gehennom higher than Vlad's top level.
Vlad's Tower -> Dungeons of Doom.

> If so, how do you specify levels in other branches, e.g. Minetown?

You don't. (Outside wizard mode, where there is a menu available to do
so.) Interbranch teleport is simply a consequence of picking a level
number shallower than your current branch contains, or deeper in the
special case of teleport to the Valley.

> If not, why not? :-)

Because that's the way level teleport works; if you want to be able to
visit other branches, that's what the Eye of the Aethiopica is for.

(The DevTeam acknowledge in the source that the current handling of
branches that extend in different directions, while consistent, is not
ideal. But it's what we've got.)

